{"id":"b1d7e015-7d40-44b6-8d5c-832a58ed9130","object":"chat.completion","created":1795147706,"model":"deepseek-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"SELECT ps.customer_state,\n       ROUND(AVG(ps.person_product_amount), 2) AS avg_product_amount_per_person\nFROM (\n    SELECT c.customer_state,\n           c.customer_unique_id,\n           SUM(oi.price) AS person_product_amount\n    FROM orders o\n    JOIN customers c ON c.customer_id = o.customer_id\n    JOIN order_items oi ON oi.order_id = o.order_id\n    GROUP BY c.customer_state, c.customer_unique_id\n) ps\nGROUP BY ps.customer_state\nORDER BY ps.customer_state\nLIMIT 100;","reasoning_content":"We need answer SQL only. Need interpret. Need produce one SELECT. Chinese question:\n\n\"按订单对应客户档案所在州，统计有商品明细的下单自然人的人均商品金额，不含运费，全部订单状态；同人在各州分别去重。\"\n\nTranslate: By state of customer record corresponding to order, calculate per-person average product amount for ordering natural persons who have product details, excluding freight, all order statuses; same person deduplicated separately in each state.\n\nNeed SQL. Need determine metrics. We need use orders, order_items, customers. Need group by customer_state. Need average product amount per natural person (customer_unique_id) with product details. All order statuses (no filter). \"有商品明细的下单自然人\" means natural persons who placed orders with order_items (orders that have item details), likely include those orders. Per natural person total product amount = sum(oi.price) per state customer_unique_id? Then avg across natural persons per state. Need \"同人在各州分别去重\": same customer_unique_id counted separately per state; if same natural person has records in multiple states, compute separately in each state. Need be careful to avoid order_items duplicate amplification if multiple customers? Each order has one customer_id. Natural person can have multiple customer records, orders associated with customer_id. For each order, state is customer record of that order. Person total in a state should sum item prices for orders placed by any of that person's customer records in that state? \"按订单对应客户档案所在州\" state from order's customer record. \"同人在各州分别去重\" means group state, unique person within state. So for each state + customer_unique_id, sum product amount across that person's orders whose customer record state = state. Then average across persons per state. Need include only persons with product details. Since summing order_items, any order with item details contributes. Persons with no order_items excluded naturally via inner join. \"有商品明细的下单自然人\" maybe need ensure orders with items; not all orders. We can JOIN order_items.\n\nNeed decide whether use order_items.price sum directly per state/customer_unique_id, then average. Need not count duplicate items? order_items rows are item lines; sum price correct. Need avoid duplicate if multiple order_items. Summing is correct. Need group by state, customer_unique_id in subquery, then average of person totals per state.\n\nSQL:\n\nSELECT c.customer_state,\n       ROUND(AVG(person_sales.total_amount), 2) AS avg_product_amount_per_person\nFROM (\n  SELECT c.customer_state, c.customer_unique_id, SUM(oi.price) AS total_amount\n  FROM orders o\n  JOIN customers c ON c.customer_id = o.customer_id\n  JOIN order_items oi ON oi.order_id = o.order_id\n  GROUP BY c.customer_state, c.customer_unique_id\n) person_sales\nGROUP BY c.customer_state\nORDER BY c.customer_state;\n\nNeed column alias maybe avg_price? User asked \"人均商品金额\". Use avg_product_amount. Need LIMIT because rule 3: must LIMIT except single row no group COUNT etc. Since GROUP BY, include LIMIT? Hard rule says must LIMIT; so add LIMIT maybe 100? But top? Not asked top. Need output all states? \"按州\" likely all states. But must LIMIT; can LIMIT 100? State count maybe 27. Use LIMIT 100 or 1000. Default TopN only if asked. For all states, LIMIT 100 is okay to satisfy. Maybe LIMIT 1000. Need no ORDER? Could order state. Add ORDER BY c.customer_state LIMIT 100. Is that acceptable? It may truncate if >100 states but Brazil states ~27. Fine. Could use LIMIT 1000. Need exact.\n\nNeed think if \"有商品明细的下单自然人\" means natural persons (customer_unique_id) who have orders with product details. Yes.\n\nPotential nuance: Same natural person has multiple customer_ids in same state? group by state, customer_unique_id sums all. Fine. Same person in different states: each state group computed from orders' customer records state; person appears in multiple state groups. Good.\n\nCould there be orders with no customer? no.\n\nNeed include \"全部订单状态\" no status filter. Good.\n\nNeed not add freight. Use price only. Good.\n\nNeed maybe \"商品金额\" could mean sum(price) not including freight. Yes.\n\nNeed average rounded 2. Use AVG numeric. Subquery sum numeric. AVG numeric returns numeric; ROUND okay.\n\nNeed no comment? Rule 18 allows complex multi-table comment, not necessary. Only SQL.\n\nCheck if need use customer_unique_id for natural person. Yes. Since state from order corresponding customer record, use c.customer_state and c.customer_unique_id. If same person has multiple customer records in state, sum across all orders in that state. Great.\n\nNeed if an order has multiple item rows and same person multiple orders; sum. Average over persons. Good.\n\nNeed \"同人在各州分别去重\": within each state dedup person via group by. Good.\n\nPotential issue: If the same order has multiple customer records? No order has one customer_id. If customer_unique_id same across multiple customer_ids, orders by same natural person but different customer records. State group based on each order's record. Good.\n\nLet's formulate final. Must only SELECT. Include LIMIT. Use aliases lower? SQL no quotes. Table columns lower. Could alias \"avg_product_amount\". Need perhaps \"avg_item_amount_per_person\".\n\nFinal:\nSELECT c.customer_state,\n       ROUND(AVG(ps.person_product_amount), 2) AS avg_product_amount_per_person\nFROM (\n    SELECT c.customer_state,\n           c.customer_unique_id,\n           SUM(oi.price) AS person_product_amount\n    FROM orders o\n    JOIN customers c ON c.customer_id = o.customer_id\n    JOIN order_items oi ON oi.order_id = o.order_id\n    GROUP BY c.customer_state, c.customer_unique_id\n) ps\nJOIN customers c? Wait subquery has c alias, outer cannot reference c.customer_state unless alias ps. Outer SELECT should ps.customer_state. Yes.\n\nSELECT ps.customer_state, ROUND(AVG(ps.person_product_amount), 2) ...\nFROM (...) ps\nGROUP BY ps.customer_state\nORDER BY ps.customer_state\nLIMIT 100;\n\nYes.\n\nNeed consider if \"有商品明细的下单自然人\" requires an order with product details; JOIN order_items ensures at least one item. Good.\n\nNeed if order_items price null? likely no. AVG of sum. Fine.\n\nLet's final."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":3563,"completion_tokens":1539,"total_tokens":5102,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":1792},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":1410},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":1792,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":1771},"system_fingerprint":"bc19ba97cbe016479903222bb1578db6"}